15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a systematic review process with four stages: identification, screening, eligibility, and inclusion. Initial records total four thousand two hundred two, duplicates removed yielding three thousand two hundred ninety-nine, two thousand eight hundred ninety-four excluded after screening, four hundred five full-text reviewed, and thirty-two publications included.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Bar chart illustrating risk of bias by category in green for low risk, yellow for unclear risk, and red for high risk. Most categories display predominantly low risk of bias, with slight unclear or high risk present in certain areas, specifically allocation concealment and incomplete outcome data. A color-coded key defines each risk type.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Eight network diagrams labeled A through H illustrate treatment comparisons in clinical studies. Each diagram features nodes representing treatments, with thicker lines indicating more frequent or robust comparisons. Placebo is a central large blue node in each network, connected via black lines to multiple other treatments such as belimumab, baricitinib, and others, with each treatment forming smaller peripheral blue nodes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a matrix comparing telitacicept, IL-2, belimumab, ILT-101, tabalumab, blisibimod, and placebo treatments with relative effect sizes and confidence intervals. Panel B displays a similar matrix for ustekinumab, ABBV-599 high-dose, deucravacitinib, anifrolumab, upadacitinib, sifalimumab, iberdomide, atacicept, PF04236921, dapirolizumab pegol, evobrutinib, baricitinib, epratuzumab, and placebo, presenting pairwise comparisons of treatments with effect sizes and confidence intervals. Bold values highlight statistically significant results.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
